  {
    label: 'India-specific hiring signal',
    text: 'The India Skills Report 2026 puts graduate employability at 56.35%, up from 54.81% the year before, and lists AI and data analytics, cloud computing and cybersecurity among the skills in highest demand.',
    read: 'Read it as: employability is improving, but more than four in ten test-takers still fall short of an employer\'s bar. It is a test-based measure, not a job guarantee.',
  },
  {
    label: 'LinkedIn Skills on the Rise, India 2026',
    text: 'LinkedIn names five rising skill stacks for India: AI and automation, data and analytics, IT and cybersecurity, business and growth, and people and leadership. It also reports that 74% of Indian recruiters find it hard to find qualified talent, while 38% of Indian job seekers feel unprepared for the pace of technology change.',
    read: 'Read it as: the market is asking for stacks (a technical skill plus a people or business skill), not single labels.',
