  <h2 id="related">Where this differs from nearby pages</h2>

  <p>
    A few nearby pages answer related questions. Here is what each one does that this page does not.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><a href="/blog/skills/best-skills-for-high-salary-in-india/">Best skills for high salary in India</a> ranks skills by pay. This page starts from your blocker, so the right answer can be a low-cost skill that unlocks the next step.</li>
    <li><a href="/blog/skills/high-income-skills-without-a-degree-india/">High-income skills without a degree</a> is for people choosing a route without a degree. This page assumes you have a starting point and need to choose what to add.</li>
    <li><a href="/blog/career-change/upskilling-for-career-change-india/">Upskilling for a career change</a> is about switching fields. This page also covers staying in your field and growing.</li>
    <li><a href="/services/assessments/skill-assessment/">Skill assessment</a> gives you a readiness signal. This page helps you turn that signal into one skill choice.</li>
    <li><a href="/services/assessments/career-development-assessment-tests/">Career development assessment tests</a> help you see where you stand today. This page explains what to build next.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      Name your blocker from the four above. Pick one skill that answers it. Run one small test and show
      it to one person in the field. That is a complete first step, and it costs very little.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    If you want a person to check your blocker, compare two or three skill options against your money,
    time and family situation, and keep guiding you as your plan changes, you can start
    <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/">career guidance</a>
    aimed at a high-income skill portfolio and earlier financial freedom. If you would rather see where
    you stand first, the free
    <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/assessments">career and skill assessments</a> are a
    quiet place to begin.
  </p>

